    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0300" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.24/96: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Drew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-16T15:00:00-05:00">May 16, 1941—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 17—9:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>88. Minister of National Defense informs me that at the suggestion of the
                    Department a military mission composed of Colonel Urrutia, the Chief of the
                    Ecuadoran Air Corps,<anchor n="79" xml:id="d239-f1"/> the Commander of the First
                    Military Zone, and a fourth officer now in the United States will go to
                    Washington the end of this month to remain for a minimum of 90 days to discuss
                    procurement of armament.</p>
                <pb facs="0301" n="293" xml:id="pg293"/>
                <p>I understood that <hi rendition="#italic">El Comercio</hi> of Lima in connection
                    with discussion of the mediation offer<anchor n="80" xml:id="d239-f2"/> has
                    already criticized our action in transferring two patrol boats to Ecuador. It
                    occurs to me that further criticism may be made when the visit of the Ecuadoran
                    Military Mission to Washington becomes known, possibly prejudicing the success
                    of the mediation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Drew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d239-f1" n="79" xml:id="d239-f1-content">
                <p>Maj. Jorge Paez.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d239-f2" n="80" xml:id="d239-f2-content">
                <p>For the negotiations concerning the Peruvian-Ecuadoran boundary dispute, see <ref
                        target="frus1941v06#pg_212">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, pp.
                        212</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
